WEBVTT

00:34:58.851 --> 00:35:02.798
and I wouldn't have done that
if the book wasn't so ferociously due.

00:35:02.822 --> 00:35:04.526
You know, my publisher had --

00:35:04.550 --> 00:35:05.981
CA: The power of a deadline.

00:35:06.005 --> 00:35:07.306
EG: It was a real deadline.

00:35:07.330 --> 00:35:10.720
And they had very graciously given me
an extra year when Rayya got sick,

00:35:10.744 --> 00:35:13.584
and not a lot of people who have jobs
get that kind of time

00:35:13.608 --> 00:35:15.805
to be able to spend
with a partner who's dying.

00:35:15.829 --> 00:35:18.312
I'm so grateful for that,
and I wanted to reward them

00:35:18.336 --> 00:35:21.496
by giving them the book that
they paid me for and that I owed them.

00:35:21.520 --> 00:35:27.360
But the deadline was very serious,
and had I been not in that deadline,

00:35:27.384 --> 00:35:30.156
I would have said, "This is
a terrible time for me to work.